# Run

run resolves one previously built kind: app artifact from the selected host or target lane and delegates command construction and execution to mm.run.

run -h

run --host apps/main -- -v

run --target apps/main -- -h

Arguments after -- belong to the application and are passed without being interpreted as run options. The host lane executes its application directly. The target lane requires a configured runner and executes the application through that runner.

run does not build an application. A missing artifact is diagnosed with an instruction to run build first. Invalid manifests, non-app manifests, and applications unavailable in the selected lane are rejected.

A configured runner and target host capability are independent. Host capability controls which nodes may be built in the target lane. A runner controls whether an artifact from that lane can be executed by this machine.
